The data economy of public proteomics over thirteen years of PRIDE
Filip Rumenovski, Wayne State University

Analysis code and frozen inputs for 36,249 public PRIDE datasets released 2013-2025.

Check the release (Python 3.12+, pinned versions in requirements.txt):

  python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
  python scripts/verify_release.py
  python scripts/release_early.py validate --data-dir data/early --output-dir results/early
  python scripts/release_late.py validate --data data/late --output results/late

Full rebuild (about 20 minutes). Download Source-metadata.zip and
Extraction-caches.zip from Zenodo (https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23870917;
mirrored as GitHub release v1.1.0), unzip them, and
install Liberation Sans (or pass --font-dir with its TTF files):

  unzip Source-metadata.zip -d SOURCE
  unzip Extraction-caches.zip -d CACHES
  python scripts/reproduce_all.py --source SOURCE --cache-dir CACHES --output OUT

All 23 stages must pass and all 79 result tables must match (OUT/Numerical-comparison.json).

